NUKED SB-EMU AWE32 Edition @VER@ - floppy install set (@N@ disks)

Same files as the release zip, packed onto 1.44 MB disks.

Install (DOS or a Windows 98 DOS box):
  1. Put disk 1 in drive A:
  2. A:\INSTALL         installs to drive C:
     A:\INSTALL D       installs to drive D:
     A:\INSTALL C B     disks are in drive B:
  3. Swap disks when asked. Every file is CRC-checked while it is unpacked;
     a bad disk is reported by number, so only that disk needs writing again.
  4. INSTALL then runs SETUP.BAT, the same as after unzipping the pack.

Needs about 25 MB free and a 386 or newer with 4 MB RAM or more.
The pack is unpacked to C:\NUKEDSB first (README.TXT is there).
Plain DOS shortens two long names: DOWNLOADS.TXT -> DOWNLOAD.TXT,
FILES\DOSMODE\CDROM-D810.TXT -> CDROM-D8.TXT.

UNPAK.EXE uses XZ Embedded (public domain / 0BSD). HDPMI32I.EXE is the
DPMI host that comes with the pack.
